===Noun===
{{en-noun|head=[[middle]] [[class]]|middle classes}}

# A [[social]] and [[economic]] [[class]] lying above the [[working class]] and below the [[upper class]].
#*{{quote-magazine|date=2013-08-10|volume=408|issue=8848|magazine={{w|The Economist}}
|title=[http://www.economist.com/news/leaders/21583277-worlds-biggest-polluter-going-green-it-needs-speed-up-transition-can-china Can China clean up fast enough?]
|passage=All this has led to an explosion of protest across China, including among a '''middle class''' that has discovered nimbyism. That worries the government, which fears that environmental activism could become the foundation for more general political opposition. It is therefore dealing with pollution in two ways—suppression and mitigation.}}
# {{qualifier|plural}} The groups in society composed of professionals, semi-professionals, and lower-to-middle managerial level workers.

